### The parent defends the child's right to refuse unwanted touching.

1 of 27 posts.

A parent of a three-year-old says older women repeatedly touch the child's curly hair without asking. When the child swats a stranger's arm away, the parent checks on the child and explains that strangers should ask first, but friends say the child should have been punished. The parent is teaching a verbal refusal that also applies to an affectionate friend.

- "I usually try to see it coming and get in front of her, because she has expressed that she doesn't like it" [ar011-0032]
- "The lady was insistent that I apologise for my daughter's "violence"." [ar011-0032]
