### The parent feels judged for not doing enough about the child's behaviour or daily care.

3 of 27 posts.

Parents of two- and three-year-olds describe a grandmother criticising skipped hygiene tasks, a relative saying children lacked discipline during a family holiday, and a friend repeatedly lecturing about playdate injuries and hitting. They describe feeling like a failure, a burden or a scolded parent despite efforts to manage care and behaviour. Some ask for reassurance, while others accept a need for closer supervision but object to being repeatedly lectured.

- "Are we the only ones who can't get our shit together? My mother's judgement is making me feel like a failure because we don't do these things." [ar040-0030]
- "I want to do these things in theory, especially the teeth, but the thought of having to force him to do more things that require that level of oversight and that he fights us on is just too much, especially when we're all trying to get ready in the AM." [ar040-0029]
- "I was so caught off guard and now it’s making me feel like an absolute shit parent who can’t control her kids, when I already felt like that." [ar015-0051]
- "This makes me not want to go there anymore… not bc I’m mad, but bc I feel like such a burden now. How are we as parents supposed to enjoy anything when you now feel like you can’t or don’t want to ask for help too much" [ar015-0052]
- "The dad is constantly watching out kid's' every move and at every play date he starts asking if we give our son enough attention and maybe we are not correcting his behavior." [ar071-0081]
- "Yes I totally understand that parents don't want their kids getting hurt by other children and yes you are right about different temperaments. U know my son is mischievous and likes to instigate and we intervene as much as we can. Maybe  giving a tip or advice is fine from the other parents is fine but what annoys me is the constant lecturing and questioning our parenting at every single outing." [ar071-0100]

**But:** These accounts do not claim that all criticism has no basis: "I want to do these things in theory, especially the teeth" [ar040-0029] "Yes hitting is worse, and it has happened twice from our visits so definitely have to supervise him better." [ar071-0096]

