### The parent wants the adults' television habits to stop disrupting the toddler's play or behaviour.

2 of 27 posts.

Parents of a two-year-old and a two-and-a-half-year-old describe television that stays on in a friend's home or in their own and the grandparents' homes. One wants a playdate without a distracting screen and has difficulty arranging an outing; the other tries outings to avoid all-day football, but is tired and asks why sports are allowed when children's programmes are limited. The latter reports that the child touches or climbs toward the television and is harder to handle around it.

- "Every time we are there the tv is constantly on. My child has limited screen time and I honestly don’t know what to do." [ar067-0121]
- "My little one is sociable but the tv is a real distraction." [ar067-0123]
