One mother describes a dispute about a son refusing a hug that exposed deeper disagreement with her husband and led to talk of separation; the son's age is not identified among her three boys aged three, five and nine. Another mother describes physically blocking an acquaintance from touching her uncomfortable two-year-old and explaining that the child's refusal counts. They want to protect bodily autonomy while asking whether their responses were excessive and how to handle adult pushback.

- "MIL said he should hug him, I said he don’t force hugs. She basically said my house, my rules. I said, my son, his body." [ar069-0018]
- "I believe it is harmful to force affection, especially from trusted adults, because it teaches them all sorts of lessons I disagree with." [ar069-0024]
- "Donc j’ai pour la première fois et j’en suis fière, mît la main en avant, j’ai reculé d’un pas, et j’ai dit « ah non, elle n’aime pas qu’on la touche »" [ar073-0105]
- "En réponse j’ai un haussement de sourcil vertigineux, avec un « ah bon ?? », plus aucun sourire, la tronche en biais, et elle se casse en me disant « c’est pas elle qui a eu un mouvement de recul, là, c’est vous »" [ar073-0106]
