4:('Disputes concern Catholic teaching, taking museum toys and an accidentally rude hand gesture.',[q(4,0,'She also asked to take my daughter to her church group and I said no.'),q(4,2,'While we were my MIL basically stole one of the toys from the play area. She pulled it out of her pocket while I was buckling my child into her seat and gave it to her.'),q(4,6)],'Learning about religion is acceptable: '+b(4,'I’m fine with my daughter learning about religion at this age, but I’d rather it be in the context that there are many different belief systems.','ar074-0027')),
5:('The parent supports a three-year-old resisting strangers touching her hair and teaches verbal refusal.',[q(5,1),q(5,2)],'The father agrees: '+b(5,'My husband says I did absolutely the right thing','ar011-0032')),
6:('Hygiene, holiday behaviour and playdate injuries draw criticism despite parents’ efforts.',[q(6,0),q(6,4)],'Some accept a need to change: '+b(6,'Yes hitting is worse, and it has happened twice from our visits so definitely have to supervise him better.','ar071-0096')),
7:('Parents managing a lobby meltdown or singing on a flight question strangers’ expectations.',[q(7,0),q(7,3)],'The singing disturbed someone: '+b(7,'Then, the woman sitting in front of him turns around and says can we please do something about him because he woke her up.','ar029-0057')),
8:('One resists overanxious grandparents; another objects to a friend encouraging running against handholding rules.',[q(8,0),q(8,3,'My child is 2 and is a runner , I’m trying to teach him to walk next to me nicely without hand holding , he’s currently really good at holding hands and knows if he’s out the pram he has to hold my hand unless we are at the park etc.')],'One questions their judgement: '+b(8,'I had enough that day and finally told her this stuff but I do wonder if maybe my bike polo/skateboarding days have clouded my judgment of the gnarr.','ar070-0027')),
9:('Parents seek screen-free playdates or relief from all-day football.',[q(9,1),q(9,3,'Now that football is back, I’ve been trying to keep my son out of the house on the weekends but I am getting tired.')],'The playdate also involves limited shared play: '+b(9,'Doesn’t communicate yet, doesn’t really play with toys, doesn’t join in etc','ar067-0126')),
10:('Parents question staff’s language about toilet learning, fear and regulation, including during settling-in.',[q(10,1),q(10,4)],'One praises the provision: '+b(10,'It is a solid quality daycare with fewer kids, more attention and resources, but she is having a difficult time.','ar057-0096')),
11:('Black parents in Utah say CPS reported bathroom isolation and staff mocking and photographing their toddler after sunscreen; they did not witness these incidents.',[q(11,0),q(11,1,'Everything we learned today came from the CPS call. The daycare never informed us about any of these incidents.')],'One employee reportedly was dismissed: '+b(11,'We were told that the employee was eventually fired, but this supposedly happened quite a while ago, and nobody from the daycare ever mentioned it to us.','ar039-0094')),
12:('Mothers resist forced hugs or touching; one son’s age is unknown among three siblings.',[q(12,0),q(12,2)],'One reopens discussion of visits: '+b(12,'I have relaxed my decision about them not seeing his parents and have told him I am open to discussing how they could see them in person.','ar069-0025')),
13:('A mother asks her husband to manage anger and stop expecting older-child emotional control.',[q(13,0,'My husband treats our toddler like he is older than he is.'),q(13,3)],'She reports some improvement: '+b(13,'He seems to take the feedback and tries to improve, but I am concerned by exposing our children to this behavior they will be impacted negatively.','ar067-0064')),
14:('Parents object to skipped kindergarten routines or whole packs of gummies instead of single potty-training rewards.',[q(14,1),q(14,3)],'The routine still needs prompting: '+b(14,'When she is with me she definitely still needs prompting from time to time but she gets her little routine done after school.','ar070-0149')),
15:('Parents defend comforting a toddler after a crib transition and a six-month-old with painful conditions.',[q(15,1),q(15,5)],'The toddler previously slept independently: '+b(15,'Just put her in her crib and she went to sleep on her own.','ar031-0028')),
16:('Parents dispute criticism about support for suspected autism and ask grandparents to address both parents directly.',[q(16,1,'We have largely maxed out our insurance and are waiting for a diagnosis to be able to do more therapies.'),q(16,2)],'Grandparents provide care and report feeling intimidated: '+b(16,'He cited an example of when something happens (like a kid falls or I trip over something) his reaction can be intense when he is trying to figure out what happened.','ar035-0109')),
17:('A mother feels judged over work, preschool, vaccination and public school. The vaccine/autism claim is the friend’s reported statement.',[q(17,0),q(17,1)],'She acknowledges different choices: '+b(17,'I understand that she has a right to parent her child the way she thinks is best, however, I don’t like the feeling of judgement that comes along with the choices I have made as a parent.','ar059-0019')),
18:('Repeated questioning damages the parent’s mental health; efforts to talk bring little response.',[q(18,1),q(18,2)],'The wife also questions the relationship: '+b(18,\"She texted me today after I took my son to daycare that she's staying home for a mental health day and basically told me she's wondering if our relationship is OK and didnt say anything else\",'ar036-0065')),
19:('Initially posing as a parent, the speaker identifies as the friend receiving the replies. The child’s age is unknown.',[q(19,0),q(19,1,'Another predetermined response the son offered to the question was \"you\\'re chubby.\"')],'nothing found against it.'),
20:('The parent objects to aggressive cheering and comparing elementary-school children; exact ages are unknown.',[q(20,0),q(20,1)],'Some enjoy it: '+b(20,'the few kids at the lead are having a good day. the top few boys and girls are rewarded.','ar048-0024')),
21:('A coach rejects personally funding medals; ages are unknown and costs are hypothetical.',[q(21,0,\"She went on to say that because another coach in the same league had bought medals for his team - I should buy for our team so her older child isn't left out.\"),q(21,1,'That would be like "'$1000 at $5 per medal out of my pocket.'"')],'nothing found against it.'),
}
